+    Rule:
+    - For each arrow, start at its missing corner and cast a diagonal ray in that corner's direction.
+    - If the diagonal next cell is a wall, reverse both direction components; otherwise if only one axial side cell is a wall, reverse that axis only.
+    - After applying any bounce, move one diagonal step; stop before stepping out of bounds or into another arrow body, and count how many bounces occurred.
